# Gherkin Feature Template

Generate exactly one observable scenario per requirements acceptance criterion. Give every scenario one distinct stable `@SCN...` tag. Generated file content consists only of required frontmatter, file/source comments, a Feature line, and AC-linked observable scenarios. Do not emit authoring instructions, section dividers, step-definition guidance, feasibility data, or external obligations inside the generated file.

## Feature Variant

```gherkin
**Issue**: #[number]
**Date**: [YYYY-MM-DD]
**Status**: Draft | Approved
**Author**: [name]
**Related Spec**: specs/{M}-{slug}/

# File: {test-layer}/features/[feature-name].feature
# Generated from: specs/{N}-{slug}/requirements.md
Feature: [Feature Name]

  @SCN001
  Scenario: [AC1 observable scenario name]
    Given [AC1 software precondition]
    When [AC1 user or system action]
    Then [AC1 observable outcome]

  @SCN002
  Scenario: [AC2 observable scenario name]
    Given [AC2 software precondition]
    When [AC2 action]
    Then [AC2 observable outcome]
```

## Defect Variant

Use when the GitHub issue has the `bug` label. Keep the same one-scenario-per-AC rule; `@regression` may accompany, but never replace, the unique stable `@SCN...` tag.

```gherkin
**Issue**: #[number]
**Date**: [YYYY-MM-DD]
**Status**: Draft | Approved
**Author**: [name]
**Related Spec**: specs/{M}-{slug}/

# File: {test-layer}/features/[feature-name].feature
# Generated from: specs/{N}-{slug}/requirements.md
Feature: [Bug summary]

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: [AC1 bug no longer reproduces]
    Given [the software condition that triggered the bug]
    When [the action that caused incorrect behavior]
    Then [the observable correct behavior]

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: [AC2 related behavior is preserved]
    Given [a related working condition]
    When [the related action occurs]
    Then [the observable existing behavior remains]
```

Authoring rules:

- Preserve direct one-to-one AC/scenario mapping and unique stable tags.
- Use concrete repository-domain examples and independent scenarios.
- Add `Background:` only for shared software preconditions.
- Describe observable behavior, not implementation procedure.
- Omit legal or policy rationale, ownership proof, approval or attestation, live operations, delivery controls, and instructional prose from generated Gherkin.
